## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end design for long-form audio with multi-chapter outputs, requiring integration of Transcribe, SageMaker, OpenSearch, and DynamoDB, plus governance, privacy, and cross-account considerations.

## Key Concepts

- AWS Transcribe: language auto-detect, diarization
- Time-based chunking of transcripts
- SageMaker endpoint for per-chapter summaries
- OpenSearch and DynamoDB indexing for chapter search
- S3 storage with timestamped prefixes and encryption
- Data lineage with Glue and auditing/tracking
- Cross-account access, IAM least-privilege, DLQ, cost controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: chunk transcript, call SageMaker per chapter, write outputs
async function processChapteredTranscript(transcript) {
  const chapters = chunkByTime(transcript);
  for (const c of chapters) {
    const summary = await sageMaker.summarize(c.text);
    await s3.put(`episode/${transcript.episodeId}/${c.start}-${c.end}.txt`, c.text);
    await s3.put(`episode/${transcript.episodeId}/${c.start}-${c.end}.summary.txt`, summary);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How do you ensure idempotent re-processing for re-uploaded files?
- What operational metrics and alerts would you set for cost and quality drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design a compliant, scalable machine-learning data pipeline with end-to-end governance and drift controls.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven orchestration (S3/EventBridge/Step Functions)
- Privacy: KMS, encryption at rest, access logs
- Data lineage: Glue Data Catalog
- Governance: Lake Formation
- ML inference: SageMaker endpoint, model drift monitoring
- Cross-account sharing and cost controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js: SageMaker endpoint invocation sketch
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const sage = new AWS.SageMakerRuntime();
async function classify(input){
  const res = await sage.invokeEndpoint({EndpointName:'ml-endpoint', Body: JSON.stringify(input), ContentType:'application/json'}).promise();
  return JSON.parse(res.Body.toString());
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design drift detection metrics and alerting for the SageMaker model?
- What rollback strategy would you implement if the endpoint drifts or data governance policy changes?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end real-time pipeline design, AI inference integration, privacy controls, and cost trade-offs in production-scale systems.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven architecture and streaming integration (WebSocket, Kinesis, Lambda)
- SageMaker endpoint invocation and model monitoring
- PII redaction strategies and compliance (encryption, access controls, retention)
- Data lake indexing (S3, DynamoDB) and cost implications

## Code Example

```javascript
import { SageMakerRuntimeClient, InvokeEndpointCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-sagemaker-runtime";

const client = new SageMakerRuntimeClient({ region: 'us-east-1' });

async function analyze(message){
  const cmd = new InvokeEndpointCommand({
    EndpointName: 'chat-sentiment-intent',
    ContentType: 'text/plain',
    Body: message
  });
  const res = await client.send(cmd);
  return JSON.parse(res.Body.toString());
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test privacy controls and retention policies end-to-end?
- How would you handle backpressure and scale Lambda consumptions?
- What monitoring would you add for model drift and data leakage risk?
